1
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,660
Hello everyone, welcome back to our IELTS writing course.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,740
We all know that coming up with ideas is hard, but proving them is even harder.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:25,700
In our last lesson, we mastered the topic sentence and the explanation.

4
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,960
But what if the examiner still isn't convinced?

5
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,940
That is where the example comes in.

6
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,960
Today, we will learn exactly how to use

7
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:39,660
specific real-world cases to make your arguments undeniable.

8
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,760
We'll learn the difference between an explanation and

9
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,360
an example, and I'll show you a simple

10
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:48,780
four-step formula to write perfect examples every time.

11
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,120
Let's get started.

12
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:57,200
First of all, I want to challenge you a bit.

13
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,880
I will send you a paragraph, and within

14
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:05,300
a maximum of two minutes, please read this

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,600
paragraph and identify the components within it, 

16
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,240
corresponding to the functions we've learned up to now.

17
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:19,240
The topic sentence, the explanation, the example, and elaboration.

18
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,700
Please pause the video to do this task,

19
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,800
as this is an important step before moving

20
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,800
on to the next part of the lesson.

21
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,420
See you in a bit.

22
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:39,190
We can see that this paragraph is structured as follows.

23
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:44,300
So, we have two explanations.

24
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:50,340
Explanation 1, one major concern is air pollution.

25
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:56,620
Explanation 2, another issue is deforestation, where more

26
00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:00,560
and more trees are being cut down and forests are disappearing.

27
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:06,130
Let's consider the relationship between these two sentences

28
00:02:06,130 --> 00:02:08,070
and others in the paragraph.

29
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:13,850
The topic sentence is, there are many serious environmental issues today.

30
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:21,630
With the topic, serious environmental issues, and the controlling idea is many.

31
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:26,510
We can see that two explanations develop the

32
00:02:26,510 --> 00:02:30,850
controlling idea while following the topic of the topic sentence.

33
00:02:31,850 --> 00:02:35,810
The controlling idea here is many, and 

34
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:44,210
we immediately see two different environmental problems mentioned, air pollution and deforestation.

35
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:51,520
After explanation 1 is an example.

36
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:55,460
Human actions like burning coal and oil in

37
00:02:55,460 --> 00:03:00,140
factories and driving vehicles release harmful smoke into the air.

38
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:05,040
This example specifies the idea of the explanation,

39
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:11,100
which is human actions producing harmful smoke, 

40
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:15,300
specifically burning coal and oil in factories and driving vehicles.

41
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:19,920
In other words, the explanation will generalize

42
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:22,780
the idea of the example into a bigger one

43
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,780
in case you want to start with 

44
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:27,660
the example and then provide its explanation.

45
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:31,020
We'll go into example in the next lesson,

46
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:34,160
but for now, you can imagine the relationship

47
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:38,680
between the three types of sentences in this paragraph like this.

48
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:48,460
Basically, the controlling idea in the topic sentence

49
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,880
will be explained more clearly in the explanation,

50
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:58,540
and the information in the explanation will be specified further by the example.

51
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:05,040
The topic sentence carries the main idea or the biggest idea of the paragraph.

52
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:11,100
Slightly smaller is explanation, and the smallest is the example.

53
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:17,899
After explanation 2 is not a specific example, but an elaboration.

54
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:23,880
This elaboration explains how serious deforestation is, which is.

55
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:27,700
This has a significant impact on the habitats

56
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:32,640
of many animals and plants, leading to more frequent natural disasters.

57
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:37,980
So elaboration will add more details to explanation,

58
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:41,840
but not give a specific case like example.

59
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:50,000
In a paragraph, as long as there are both functions, explanation and example is fine.

60
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:55,400
Each explanation does not necessarily have an accompanying example.

61
00:04:56,580 --> 00:05:02,400
Sometimes just adding more details by elaboration, like we have here, is enough.

62
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:06,540
Let's summarize the features of explanation.

63
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:11,620
The explanation develops the controlling idea while following

64
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,460
the topic of the topic sentence.

65
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:18,520
The explanation generalizes the idea of the example,

66
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:22,960
giving a specific case and or the elaboration,

67
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:27,080
adding more details, but not giving a specific case.

68
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,020
Example is the part where you need to

69
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:36,720
give specific cases to support your arguments.

70
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:40,660
This plays an important role in IELTS writing

71
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:45,760
tasks 2, because examples make our arguments more convincing.

72
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:51,000
If the essay only includes explanations and elaborations,

73
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:55,060
examiners may not feel convinced enough because 

74
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:59,060
there are no specific cases or real situations to support it.

75
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:03,780
Everything is just theory or personal opinions of the writers.

76
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:09,120
Examples help our essays meet the questions requirements.

77
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:13,740
Writing tasks to questions always require you to

78
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:17,220
give reasons for your answers and include any

79
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:20,920
relevant examples from your own knowledge and experience.

80
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:29,300
However, many students often struggle to differentiate between explanation and example.

81
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:33,300
This means they're confused about when to write

82
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:36,060
an explanation and when to give an example.

83
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:39,020
I have a topic sentence as follows.

84
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:42,880
Qualifications are essential for numerous reasons.

85
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,960
Let's take a look at the next two sentences.

86
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:51,540
A degree or certificate can indicate whether

87
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:55,000
a person possesses the knowledge and skills needed for a task.

88
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:59,400
A doctor requires a university degree along with

89
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,780
several years of training to provide treatments to patients.

90
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:07,280
In your opinion, which sentence is the example

91
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:10,200
and which one is the explanation?

92
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,440
I'll give you a hint.

93
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:17,980
Remember the steps for writing an explanation we learned in the previous lesson.

94
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:22,040
With that in mind, you'll find the answer more quickly.

95
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,340
I'll give you 30 seconds to answer.

96
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,040
Are you ready?

97
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:30,380
And the timer starts now!

98
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:33,900
Let me quickly remind you the three steps

99
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,340
for writing an explanation.

100
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:41,280
Step 1. Identify the topic and controlling idea in the topic sentence.

101
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:48,960
Step 2. Write the Explanation by developing the Controlling idea while following the Topic. 

102
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:53,840
And step 3. Review the explanation to see if it can

103
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:57,900
be further developed with more details or specific examples.

104
00:07:58,980 --> 00:08:02,280
Apply it to this exercise and we have

105
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:06,380
in the topic sentence, the topic is qualifications

106
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:11,880
and the controlling ideas are essential and numerous

107
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:15,440
reasons, which means the whole paragraph will discuss

108
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:18,680
some reasons why the qualifications are important.

109
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:24,560
The explanation needs to develop this controlling idea while following the topic.

110
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:31,580
This means the explanation has to provide one reason why the qualifications are important.

111
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:35,960
The first sentence is, a degree or certificate

112
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,179
can indicate whether a person possesses the knowledge

113
00:08:39,179 --> 00:08:41,140
and skills needed for a task.

114
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:45,120
This is a reason for the importance of qualifications.

115
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:50,680
So, the first sentence meets the requirement of an explanation.

116
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:55,420
Next, we review the explanation to see if

117
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:59,540
it can be further developed with more details or specific examples.

118
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:08,260
We can see that it only mentioned a general reason without any specific examples such as

119
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:16,500
a person who needs to get qualifications for work or a job which requires qualifications

120
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:19,600
to help readers understand the importance of qualifications.

121
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,800
And this became clearer in the second sentence

122
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:29,380
because a doctor was mentioned to support  the argument in the previous sentence.

123
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:33,200
Just saying someone needs a qualification isn't as

124
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:36,380
convincing as saying a doctor needs one because

125
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:41,600
being a doctor requires specialized knowledge which is shown by the qualification.

126
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,180
So, the answer is now very clear.

127
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:50,660
The first sentence is explanation and the second one is example.

128
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:55,160
Once we've identified them, we'll add linking words

129
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,920
to show their functions like, for example.

130
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:07,010
Through this exercise, we can differentiate between explanations and examples as follows.

131
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:16,320
Now, let's learn how to write an example effectively.

132
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:17,680
Let's go!

133
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:26,980
Through the previous differentiation, we can conclude that

134
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:31,420
the example will narrow down the explanation to a specific case.

135
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:39,340
Therefore, we have four steps to write an example effectively.

136
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:45,260
Step one, identify the subject that needs to be specified in the explanation.

137
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:49,380
Step two, find a specific case that is

138
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:51,580
broadly representative of the subject.

139
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:55,980
Step three, begin the sentence with a phrase

140
00:10:55,980 --> 00:11:02,080
indicating example and present the case followed by an elaboration if needed.

141
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:08,080
And step four, review the example that you've written according to the checklist.

142
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:10,960
Let's analyze each step together.

143
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:16,920
Step one, identify the subject that needs to be specified in the explanation.

144
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:22,460
I have a topic sentence and an explanation as follows.

145
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:27,120
Academic qualifications are not always necessary.

146
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:31,280
To begin with, some jobs prioritize practical skills

147
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:35,340
and experience over knowledge obtained from schools and universities.

148
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,080
Let's start with a question.

149
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,980
In the explanation, which subject can be further specified?

150
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:47,920
In an explanation, there can be many subjects that you can illustrate.

151
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:51,200
But remember to choose the subject you find

152
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:54,840
easy to provide convincing examples based on your

153
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,360
knowledge and experience.

154
00:11:56,940 --> 00:12:01,520
For example, this sentence mentioned some jobs where

155
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:06,840
practical skills and experience are more important than knowledge from schools and universities.

156
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:11,700
We can immediately think of a specific job to support this argument.

157
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,920
This is the detail that helps us  to find an example.

158
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:20,380
Step two, find a specific case that is

159
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:22,620
broadly representative of the subject.

160
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,340
Let's choose the job dancers.

161
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:28,540
This is a job where knowledge is important,

162
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:33,940
but surely not as important as practice skills and real-life experience.

163
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:38,260
Step three, begin the sentence with a phrase

164
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:44,080
indicating example and present the case followed by an elaboration if needed.

165
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:49,180
Now we will write the example and an elaboration if needed.

166
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:55,580
However, please remember, only write one elaboration to support the example.

167
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:59,180
If an example needs too much information to

168
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:03,000
make it clear, this shows the example is not convincing enough.

169
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:06,960
Instead, we should choose examples that require little

170
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:12,080
or even no elaboration, but still persuade the reader from the first read.

171
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,400
Let's begin our sentence with a phrase indicating

172
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:19,460
example, such as for example or for instance.

173
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:24,140
I have an example about the job dancers as follows.

174
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:28,380
For example, dancers do not require a degree

175
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:30,700
to excel in their stage performances.

176
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:35,960
I need to emphasize that having qualifications is

177
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:39,420
helpful for dancers as they can find jobs more easily.

178
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:43,140
But to truly impress the audience with a

179
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:47,380
performance, the qualifications are not the most important here.

180
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,380
This sentence is already easy to understand and

181
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,420
convincing, so we don't need any elaboration.

182
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:57,240
Let's put it in a paragraph with the

183
00:13:57,240 --> 00:14:01,000
topic sentence and explanation, so you can see the relationships.

184
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:04,980
Academic qualifications are not always necessary.

185
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:08,880
To begin with, some jobs prioritize practical skills

186
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:12,560
and experience over knowledge obtained from schools and universities.

187
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,640
For example, dancers do not require a degree

188
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,860
to excel in their stage performances.

189
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:23,520
Finally, we move to step four, review the example.

190
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,200
Once you have written your sentence, you must

191
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:29,860
check it against three key criteria to ensure it will score well.

192
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,980
First, is it specific?

193
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,780
It should name a concrete job, place or

194
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:39,260
situation like dancers, rather than just general people.

195
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,600
Second, is it relevant?

196
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:45,040
Does it directly prove the explanation you just wrote?

197
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:47,340
And third, is it universal?

198
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:51,660
Avoid personal stories like my uncle or my friend.

199
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:57,440
Good IELTS examples represent a group of people or society in general.

200
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,680
If your example checks these three boxes, 

201
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:04,000
it is strong, convincing, and ready for your essay.

202
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:07,780
And that brings us to the end of today's lesson on the example.

203
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:11,380
To summarize, we learned that while an explanation

204
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:16,640
expands on your main idea generally,  an example proves it with specific evidence.

205
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:21,020
We also mastered the four-step strategy, 

206
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:25,600
identifying the subject to illustrate, finding a representative case,

207
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,060
writing the sentence using linkers like for instance,

208
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,640
and reviewing it against our checklist.

209
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:34,980
By applying this structure, you ensure that 

210
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:38,780
your arguments are not just theories, but convincing proofs.

211
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,860
Thank you for joining me and good luck with your writing practice.

